# Every text file is checked out with LF line endings, on every host.
#
# A Windows checkout otherwise converts them to CRLF, and the tree is read as
# bytes by nearly everything that gates it: the formatters report every line as
# changed, `shellcheck` refuses a literal carriage return, the schema drift test
# finds every checked-in schema differing from what the types generate, and
# `rustfmt` refuses generated code. What decides whether a file is text is git's
# own detection, so an image stays the bytes it was committed as.
* text=auto eol=lf
